  "notes": "The scheme most of the fleet still wears in 2025-2026 (777s, most A380s), being replaced by the 2023 livery (standard). The flag is flat-colored, without the 2023 ripple lines; the red runs down the rear fuselage much as on the 2023 scheme. Drawn from right-side photos plus one left-side view; belly panel from one underside photo. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on A6-ECR (777-300ER, right side, side-on, 2025-11-19; drawnOn B77W, the type most of the fleet in this scheme is), with A6-ENP's left side agreeing: 'Emirates' starts just aft of the forward door (x 0.098, it had been drawn 5.7 m further aft) and runs to 0.311, baseline about 1 m under the windows (y -0.19), capitals to y 0.47, lowercase 0.66 of the E; 'www.emirates.com' under its middle, x 0.148 to 0.234; the Arabic x 0.323 to 0.398 level with the windows' tops. The red sweep is 3 to 4 m further aft than first drawn on the 777: it leaves the crown at x 0.834 to 0.854, crosses the window line at 0.81 to 0.83 and ends in a point at x 0.721, y -0.54; smooth. On the A380 the titles sit further aft as shares.",
  "history": "Introduced in November 1999 with the first 777-300 (Wikipedia, 'Second livery'); the red belly title added in 2005; superseded by the 2023 livery, standard, and repainted as aircraft go through retrofits.",
  "commonest": true,
